On the infographic image output, the 'PLACEMENTS + EMBEDDED' section currently shows one combined set of 3 boxes (added/removed/modified). Split into two separate counts: placements and embedded, each with its own +/-/modified numbers. Rework the single row of 3 boxes into a 2-column layout, one row of 3 per group, e.g.:\n\n  : placements                             : : embedded                                 :\n  : [ X added ] [ Y removed ] [ Z modified ] : : [ A added ] [ B removed ] [ C modified ] :\n\nCreativity in exact styling is welcome. Related constraint (general note): there is NO required aspect ratio for the image - a long infographic is fine and preferred over cramming; use vertical space freely to fit all required sections legibly.